{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01LfwVNfdTpJ1veq1ai46KG8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SRGLLehwAFQpdSZmrrjRbU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr create --title \"bug: #17 - Error when acquiring PDF invoices from google drive\" --body \"## Summary\n\nThis PR fixes the Google Drive credentials JSON parsing error that prevented PDF invoices from being downloaded in the Finanzas module for Mexico.\n\n**Issue**: When uploading the Facturación Excel file, the ZIP generated only contained the Excel file but no PDF invoices due to a JSON parsing error: \\\"Failed to parse credentials JSON: Invalid control character at: line 1 column 170 (char 169)\\\"\n\n**Root Cause**: The `GOOGLE_DRIVE_CREDENTIALS_JSON` environment variable contained unescaped newline characters (`\\n`) that were being treated as literal strings instead of actual newlines, causing JSON parsing to fail.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\nSee: [specs/20251124_bug_fix_google_drive_credentials_json_parsing.md](specs/20251124_bug_fix_google_drive_credentials_json_parsing.md)\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### Core Fix\n- **google_drive_service.py**: Added proper newline character handling by replacing literal `\\n` strings with actual newline characters before JSON parsing\n\n### Documentation\n- **backend/.env.example**: Updated with comprehensive Google Drive credentials documentation including proper formatting instructions\n\n## What Was Done\n\n- [x] Analyzed error logs to identify JSON parsing failure at character 169\n- [x] Investigated Google Drive service credential loading mechanism\n- [x] Implemented newline character replacement in credential parsing\n- [x] Added comprehensive documentation in .env.example\n- [x] Tested fix to ensure proper JSON parsing\n- [x] Verified backward compatibility with properly formatted credentials\n\n## Testing\n\nThe fix handles both scenarios:\n1. Credentials with literal \\\\n strings (common when copying from Google Cloud Console)\n2. Credentials already properly formatted with actual newlines\n\n## ADW Tracking\n\nADW ID: 4a6071d9\n\nCloses #17\" --base master","description":"Create pull request with gh CLI"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":345,"cache_read_input_tokens":35488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":345,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":525,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a595731e-0eb9-44fa-a97e-9b2c30d822ff","uuid":"f27bada5-618b-47ea-af39-169d26dd9b26"}
